1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,999
Dante Config Editor 2026.1
Prepare, review, and edit Dante presets offline.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,999
Overview Open a Dante XML file or a .dceproj project,
then review devices, channels, subscriptions, and alerts at a glance.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:19,999
Devices and channels Edit a device, its settings, and RX/TX labels.
Global actions target the devices that are not locked.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,999
Adaptable workspace Collapse the left, right, and bottom panels with
persistent arrows to give the current task more room.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:33,999
Patch matrix RX channels are rows and TX channels are columns.
One click immediately applies the selected subscription.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:41,999
Easy Patch Choose RX on the left and TX on the right, then use FLIP,
1:1 patching, or a range. Every action is applied immediately.

7
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,999
Rx-to-Tx list Filter by device or channel, review subscriptions,
and quickly change an existing assignment.

8
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:55,999
Renaming Rename devices, RX, and TX directly or as a series.
Enter, Tab, and Shift+Tab speed up entry while subscriptions stay consistent.

9
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:04,999
Device banks Keep sanitized templates with images and labels,
share a bank, then insert a new independent instance into a project.

10
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:12,999
Projects Create an offline project from a template or add a second XML.
Name conflicts and references are checked before insertion.

11
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:21,999
Labels Exchange JSON, CSV, DMT XLSX/ODS, Allen & Heath
dLive/Avantis, and Yamaha CL/QL from one Import / Export workspace.

12
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:30,999
Synoptic Arrange devices, group connections, and export SVG or PDF.
The DCE layout never changes the Dante XML.

13
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:39,999
Validation The center identifies errors, warnings, and affected items.
History and Before / after make every change easier to review.

14
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:47,999
Atomic Bomb An offline training tool: choose the categories, turn the key,
then press ARM, LOCK, and FIRE to create a deliberately difficult exercise.

15
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:54,999
Windows and macOS The Windows installer and Apple Silicon and Intel
DMGs include .NET 8, device banks, and bilingual guides.

16
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:01,999
A free project Every feature remains free. A GitHub star,
feedback, or optional PayPal support can help DCE.

17
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:08,999
Thanks to the contributors Thanks to Tobi / @togrupe for DMT and
his feedback, and to Charles Bouticourt for the Atomic Bomb idea.

18
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:15,999
Third-party tool DCE does not control a live Dante network. Keep the
original and review every important file in Dante Controller before operation.

19
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Dante Config Editor 2026.1
By Mamat
